{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a legacy-compatible web service on TCP port 8080 where /cgi-bin/report executes the supplied report and preserves its business output.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The staged script defines warehouse=west and open_orders=7. Before and after restart, HTTP requests to /cgi-bin/report returned status 200 with exactly those values rather than script source; the lifecycle socket snapshot also directly shows Python listening on TCP 8080.","evidence_ids":["cmd-46c05a513785408f","cmd-088560264ff34a89","cmd-72ffbaa5475a4c9b","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep static files from public/ available at the site root.","status":"satisfied","summary":"GET / returned HTTP 200 and the staged Warehouse reports index both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-088560264ff34a89","cmd-72ffbaa5475a4c9b"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep application source and private content outside the published content.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct HTTP probes returned 404 for the private report source, the top-level handover file, and the service implementation filename before and after restart. The CGI URL returned only executed report output. The service uses public/ as its working and static-content directory.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1dbeff585db94628","cmd-088560264ff34a89","cmd-72ffbaa5475a4c9b","cmd-a23c0afd8c2e4444"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The service ran under the already-installed Python 2.7.5, was enabled and active, and recovered successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-46c05a513785408f","cmd-088560264ff34a89","cmd-72ffbaa5475a4c9b","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational